2a:["$","section","3-Keep the scholarship case distinct from the programme case",{"className":"article-section","id":"section-4","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Keep the scholarship case distinct from the programme case"}],[["$","p","Prepare an evidence map rather than one reusable essay. For an original example, a fictional applicant has strong grades in statistics, a carefully documented project on transport access and an interest in spatial methods. The course case connects preparation to particular learning needs; the scholarship case selects evidence of academic merit and commitment. The facts should agree while the emphasis answers the actual question.",{"children":"Prepare an evidence map rather than one reusable essay. For an original example, a fictional applicant has strong grades in statistics, a carefully documented project on transport access and an interest in spatial methods. The course case connects preparation to particular learning needs; the scholarship case selects evidence of academic merit and commitment. The facts should agree while the emphasis answers the actual question."}],["$","p","When the form opens, follow its live prompt, length and attachment instructions. Check each paragraph against something you can substantiate. Remove any sentence that names the wrong programme after a last-minute change of choice. Keep the final submitted copy so you can understand the decision in the context of the file actually considered.",{"children":"When the form opens, follow its live prompt, length and attachment instructions. Check each paragraph against something you can substantiate. Remove any sentence that names the wrong programme after a last-minute change of choice. Keep the final submitted copy so you can understand the decision in the context of the file actually considered."}]],"$undefined",[["$","p",null,{"className":"table-scroll-hint","children":"On a small screen, scroll the table sideways to compare all columns."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"guide-table-wrap","role":"region","aria-label":"Original evidence map for a fictional statistics applicant","tabIndex":0,"children":["$","table",null,{"className":"guide-table","children":[["$","caption",null,{"children":"Original evidence map for a fictional statistics applicant"}],["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"children":[[["$","th","True evidence",{"scope":"col","children":"True evidence"}],["$","th","Programme purpose",{"scope":"col","children":"Programme purpose"}],["$","th","Funding-case purpose",{"scope":"col","children":"Funding-case purpose"}]],"$undefined"]}]}],["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr","0",{"children":[[["$","th","0",{"scope":"row","children":"Statistics coursework"}],["$","td","1",{"children":"Shows readiness for advanced methods"}],["$","td","2",{"children":"Demonstrates sustained academic performance"}]],"$undefined"]}],["$","tr","1",{"children":[[["$","th","0",{"scope":"row","children":"Transport-access coursework project"}],["$","td","1",{"children":"Explains a specific learning gap"}],["$","td","2",{"children":"Shows careful, bounded academic work"}]],"$undefined"]}],["$","tr","2",{"children":[[["$","th","0",{"scope":"row","children":"Chosen course modules"}],["$","td","1",{"children":"Connects goals with training"}],["$","td","2",{"children":"Supports a genuine commitment to this programme"}]],"$undefined"]}]]}]]}]}],"$undefined"],"$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined"]}]
2b:["$","section","4-A tuition award still leaves a separate living budget",{"className":"article-section","id":"section-5","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"A tuition award still leaves a separate living budget"}],[["$","p","Lund’s living-cost guidance asks students to plan for both fees and living expenses. It notes that spending depends on individual circumstances and that government maintenance requirements change annually. Use the current government source for residence-permit evidence; this worksheet does not reproduce a legal minimum.",{"children":"Lund’s living-cost guidance asks students to plan for both fees and living expenses. It notes that spending depends on individual circumstances and that government maintenance requirements change annually. Use the current government source for residence-permit evidence; this worksheet does not reproduce a legal minimum."}],["$","p","Use invented figures to understand the difference. Assume annual tuition of SEK 140,000, a hypothetical 50% tuition award, living expenses of SEK 120,000 and arrival costs of SEK 10,000. Remaining tuition is SEK 70,000, so the total unfunded amount is SEK 200,000. The award has not generated SEK 70,000 cash for rent; it reduced the tuition bill.",{"children":"Use invented figures to understand the difference. Assume annual tuition of SEK 140,000, a hypothetical 50% tuition award, living expenses of SEK 120,000 and arrival costs of SEK 10,000. Remaining tuition is SEK 70,000, so the total unfunded amount is SEK 200,000. The award has not generated SEK 70,000 cash for rent; it reduced the tuition bill."}],["$","p","Now test a full-tuition scenario: the same living and arrival assumptions still leave SEK 130,000. Neither example predicts a scholarship percentage, actual Lund fees or a residence-permit amount. Replace the assumptions with your programme’s fee, documented support and your own housing plan. Keep the first payment dates visible because money promised later may not cover an early bill.",{"children":"Now test a full-tuition scenario: the same living and arrival assumptions still leave SEK 130,000. Neither example predicts a scholarship percentage, actual Lund fees or a residence-permit amount. Replace the assumptions with your programme’s fee, documented support and your own housing plan. Keep the first payment dates visible because money promised later may not cover an early bill."}]],"$undefined",[["$","p",null,{"className":"table-scroll-hint","children":"On a small screen, scroll the table sideways to compare all columns."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"guide-table-wrap","role":"region","aria-label":"Original fictional SEK funding comparison","tabIndex":0,"children":["$","table",null,{"className":"guide-table","children":[["$","caption",null,{"children":"Original fictional SEK funding comparison"}],["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"children":[[["$","th","Scenario",{"scope":"col","children":"Scenario"}],["$","th","Tuition remaining",{"scope":"col","children":"Tuition remaining"}],["$","th","Living + arrival",{"scope":"col","children":"Living + arrival"}],["$","th","Total to fund",{"scope":"col","children":"Total to fund"}]],"$undefined"]}]}],["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr","0",{"children":[[["$","th","0",{"scope":"row","children":"No award"}],["$","td","1",{"children":"140,000"}],["$","td","2",{"children":"120,000 + 10,000"}],["$","td","3",{"children":"270,000"}]],"$undefined"]}],["$","tr","1",{"children":[[["$","th","0",{"scope":"row","children":"Hypothetical 50% tuition award"}],["$","td","1",{"children":"70,000"}],["$","td","2",{"children":"130,000"}],["$","td","3",{"children":"200,000"}]],"$undefined"]}],["$","tr","2",{"children":[[["$","th","0",{"scope":"row","children":"Hypothetical full tuition award"}],"$L2d","$L2e","$L2f"],"$undefined"]}]]}]]}]}],"$undefined"],"$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$L30","$undefined"]}]
2c:["$","section","5-Review the offer as a new set of tasks",{"className":"article-section","id":"section-6","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Review the offer as a new set of tasks"}],[["$","p","Read every actual decision message for response dates, payment instructions and remaining conditions. Keep the admission and scholarship decisions together while preserving their separate tasks.",{"children":"Read every actual decision message for response dates, payment instructions and remaining conditions. Keep the admission and scholarship decisions together while preserving their separate tasks."}],["$","p","If the awarded amount differs from your planning scenario, recalculate the gap using the amount actually confirmed. Ask the university about any unclear invoice treatment rather than assuming the award is paid into your personal account. If the remaining plan cannot be funded, revisit the decision before committing to costs.",{"children":"If the awarded amount differs from your planning scenario, recalculate the gap using the amount actually confirmed. Ask the university about any unclear invoice treatment rather than assuming the award is paid into your personal account. If the remaining plan cannot be funded, revisit the decision before committing to costs."}]],"$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined",["$","nav",null,{"className":"answer-links","aria-label":"Next steps for Review the offer as a new set of tasks","children":[["$","$L5","/countries/europe/",{"href":"/countries/europe/","children":["Compare European study routes",["$","$L6",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":"$7:props:children:2:props:children:1:props:iconNode","className":"lucide-arrow-right","aria-hidden":"true"}]]}],["$","$L5","/guides/scholarship-application/",{"href":"/guides/scholarship-application/","children":["Build an application checklist",["$","$L6",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":"$7:props:children:2:props:children:1:props:iconNode","className":"lucide-arrow-right","aria-hidden":"true"}]]}],["$","$L5","/deadline-calendar/",{"href":"/deadline-calendar/","children":["Track separate application milestones",["$","$L6",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":"$7:props:children:2:props:children:1:props:iconNode","className":"lucide-arrow-right","aria-hidden":"true"}]]}]]}]]}]
